
<div class="docs-generation-mods-page">

    <div class="docs-eyebrow">MODDING SDK / WORLD GENERATION CONTRACTS</div>

    <h1>Chunk generation <span class="docs-accent">API</span></h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        The SDK defines interfaces for chunk data and generation context. The current game generation path is narrower than a complete user-extensible generator system.
    </p>

    <h2>IChunk</h2>

    <p>
        <code>Crafty.SDK.World.IChunk</code> exposes chunk X/Z coordinates, IsModified, IsRuntimeModified, IsEmpty, block read/write methods, sky/block light reads, and a light setter. The concrete game chunk implements this interface.
    </p>

    <h2>BlockPlacement</h2>

    <p>
        <code>BlockPlacement</code> is a readonly struct with a uint block ID and byte state. It is the value returned by chunk block reads and accepted by chunk block writes.
    </p>

    <h2>IChunkGenerator</h2>

    <div class="docs-code-card">
        <div class="docs-code-title">
            <span>Crafty.SDK.World.IChunkGenerator.cs</span>
            <span>ACTUAL CONTRACT</span>
        </div>

        <pre><code>public interface IChunkGenerator
{
    IChunk Generate(in ChunkGenerationContext context);
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <p>
        <code>ChunkGenerationContext</code> provides Seed, ChunkX, ChunkZ, MinY, and MaxY. The interface is a public contract, but the repository snapshot does not show a supported mod registration mechanism for replacing the game's active generator through <code>IModContext</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Current built-in generator</h2>

    <p>
        The internal <code>Crafty.ChunkGeneration.World.ChunkGenerator</code> implements the interface. It creates a concrete 32 × 416 × 32 chunk and fills each column with stone below Y=61, dirt through Y=63, and grass at Y=64. It currently does not use the seed to produce varied terrain.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not wired yet</h2>

    <ul class="docs-list">
        <li>
            <code>TerrianGenerator</code> currently throws <code>NotImplementedException</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>ChunkGenerationPipeline.Generate</code> currently throws an exception.
        </li>
        <li>
            Noise and biome generator classes are not wired into the active generation path.
        </li>
        <li>
            The SDK context does not expose a generator registry or world-generation service.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>World generation service</h2>

    <p>
        <code>IWorldGenService.GenerateWorld(worldDir, worldName, seed, progress)</code> is a service that generates a 10 × 10 chunk area in parallel and reports progress. The checked-in service should be treated as game/project infrastructure rather than a mod API unless a future SDK version explicitly exposes it.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>

        <div>
            <strong>Do not promise custom generator installation yet</strong>

            <p>
                It is accurate to say that an <code>IChunkGenerator</code> interface exists. It is not accurate to claim that third-party mods can currently register and run their own generator through a supported loader.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

